  "local_changes": "Per-file revision/path and original-source checksums are recorded below. See evidence/OSAL.md, CONNECTIONS.md, NXP-SEQUENCE.md and RF-RAW-CONFIG.md for behavioral adaptations. Raw C fragments preserve published algorithms, omit diagnostic calls, expose helpers internally, and compile through the original NXP C unit. Sequence.c changes only its PCH include to the private client ABI bridge. Core.c/CoreSend.c/TlvUtils.c omit only unlinked helpers from exact published source; CoreUtils.c retains the checksum-matched source with a local short-header length guard before its byte-2 read. Supporting Core.h init-response layout restored from PDB; unused ntassert.h removed from PCH headers. license-2015.txt and license-2016.txt retain licenses for historical pins. RawApi.inc intentionally returns INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES without context mutation on allocation failure; see docs/evidence/RAW-API-OOM-HARDENING.md. This safety change differs from original/published NULL-copy behavior. phOsalNfc.c cleans failed message-queue initialization before returning the original failure status, releasing its partial singleton; see docs/evidence/OSAL-PARTIAL-INIT-HARDENING.md. RawRfConfig.inc notifies oversized raw GET_CONFIG responses with the existing BUFFER_TOO_SMALL status and zeroed error information; see docs/evidence/RAW-QUERY-NOTIFICATION-HARDENING.md. phOsalNfc_Timer.c releases the outer deinitialization lock around Timer_Delete callback drain, then reacquires it; see docs/evidence/OSAL-TIMER-SHUTDOWN.md. This intentionally corrects the original/published recursive-lock shutdown cycle.",
